[[1789575000.0,{"slug":"akiba-lost","title":"AKIBA LOST","cover_url":"https://www.metacritic.com/a/img/catalog/provider/6/12/6-1-1157846-59.jpg","cover_source":"metacritic","cover_kind":"portrait","complete":false,"release_date":"2026-09-16","metascore":null,"userscore":null,"main_platform":"PlayStation 5","platforms":["PlayStation 5","Nintendo Switch","Nintendo Switch 2","PC"],"genres":["Action Adventure"],"developers":["IzanagiGames"],"critic_reviews":0,"user_reviews":0,"letsplay_status":"not_found","description":"13 years ago, six girls mysteriously vanished in Akihabara - an unsolved case known as “Akiba’s Spirited Away.”\r\n\r\nAt the annual Game Show, Daiki Shinjo, once hailed as a “genius creator,” boldly announces the development of a new game inspired by this very incident: AKIBA LOST. But the moment he does, strange disappearances begin again.\r\n\r\nThe cast of the game includes his sister Aoi Shinjo, who works at a maid cafe, underground idol Kokone Nagato, food writer Moe Kurosu, shrine maiden Chihiro Jimbo, cosplayer Wakana Yusa, and game streamer Yukimi Kurahashi - each a colorful icon of Akihabara’s vibrant subculture.\r\n\r\nYet, the story they were supposed to perform soon begins to bleed into reality.\r\n\r\nIt all begins with a threatening phone call - and the sudden disappearance of Aoi.\r\n\r\n\"Cancel the game’s development - or the tragedy will repeat itself.\"\r\n\r\nCan Shinjo finish developing the game? Can he protect his friends? Who is behind it all? And what really happened thirteen years ago?","description_source":"metacritic","rating":null,"publishers":["IzanagiGames"],"video_url":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/4131220/885385408/97619c96750933d6ed9e3b8ab521a363f4adb6ef/1769152784/hls_264_master.m3u8?t=1769154789","video_title":"AKIBA LOST_EN","video_source":"steam","video_poster":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/257271085/6e4dfa6b0823f64579e07a4bf12fe9c4c00e4269/movie_600x337.jp